<!--
    Somali, a draft not yet read by a fluent reviewer (#495). The notes on each string are in values/strings.xml.
    Standard Somali in the Latin alphabet, speaking to the driver as "adiga" (singular imperatives: Dooro, Bilow).
    "Vehicle" is gaari (gaariga, plural gaadiid), never the word for bus; "route" is khad (khadka 7);
    "run" is wareeg (wareegga 6:43); "trip" is safar (safarka); "stop" is joogsi; "block" is silsilad;
    "agency" is shirkad (shirkaddaada), the everyday word, where hay'ad would be the formal one;
    "dispatcher" is kormeere (kormeerahaaga); "admin" is maamule; "report" is warbixin (feminine,
    warbixinood after a number above one); "rider" is raakib, plural rakaab.
    "Sign in" is soo gal, "sign out" is ka bax; "server", "app" and "link" stay as loanwords
    (server-ka, app-ka, linkiga); "location" is goob; "connection" is internet; "diagnostics" is xogta app-ka.
    "On time" is waqtigii, "late" is daahay, "early" is hore. Minutes stay daqiiqo, which does not change
    with the number; hours are written saac, the short form used in counts such as 24 saac.
-->
